                                                "sense_id": "a9a86c13-4245-3e12-979d-33f1a7eaea70",
                                                "text": "the sheltered cot, the cultivated farm"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "157aaf2d-300b-4ce4-9f80-b0300efb1cd3",
                                                "sense_id": "a9a86c13-4245-3e12-979d-33f1a7eaea70",
                                                "text": "One evening […] we were on a sudden, greatly astonished, by hearing a violent knocking on the outward Door of our rustic Cot."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9532056f-3572-43a1-89b2-4ffa8718aedf",
                                                "sense_id": "a9a86c13-4245-3e12-979d-33f1a7eaea70",
                                                "text": "1898, Ethna Carbery, \"Roddy McCorley\" (poem).\nOh, see the fleet-foot hosts of men who speed with faces wan / From farmstead and from thresher's cot along the banks of Ban"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
